# Two branches that are correlated through global history.
# Branch 0x100 has a pseudo-random pattern that is unpredictable from its
# own history; branch 0x104 always equals the most recent outcome of
# 0x100. A global-history predictor sees 0x100's outcome inside the GHR
# when it predicts 0x104, so it can capture the correlation directly. A
# local-history predictor cannot: 0x104's own history looks just as
# random as 0x100's.
0x100 T
0x104 T
